      "card_ids": ["C05"],
      "claim": "Sembragiline, another 3-fluorobenzyloxy-substituted MAO-B inhibitor, crossed the human BBB and inhibited brain MAO-B in PET imaging, reinforcing the CNS-penetrant nature of this aryl ether scaffold.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C06"],
      "claim": "A fluorobenzyloxy-substituted cyclic compound achieved a high Brain:Blood ratio of 3.5 in rats, showing that this lipophilic ether class can achieve robust brain exposure.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "ALX-1393, an amino acid with a 3-fluorophenyl and benzyl ether, showed minimal brain penetration, but its zwitterionic amino acid character is not shared by the neutral, lipophilic query indanone, limiting transferability.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is a neutral, lipophilic 3-fluorobenzyloxy-substituted indanone. Multiple close analogs bearing the same 3-fluorobenzyloxy aryl ether motif demonstrate robust BBB penetration in human PET studies and rat brain/plasma measurements, strongly supporting meaningful CNS access.",
